[[15,1,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p><a href=\"#/2429604\">7040L40</a></p><p><a href=\"#/2429644\">7050A20</a></p><p><a href=\"#/2429642\">7050A10</a></p><p><a href=\"#/2429597\">7040H50</a>\n                                           (left\nside)</p><p><a href=\"#/2429589\">7040G30</a></p><p><a href=\"#/2429595\">7040H42</a>\n                                           (left\nside)</p><p>1. Working at the rear of the roof lining, release the cover (1a)\nand open it.</p><p>2. Undo the bolt.</p><p>3. Move the centre rear seat belt idler.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2045280.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[15,1,0,"<p>1. Undo the bolt (1a) and move the belt idler (1b).</p><p>2. Undo the bolt (2a) and keep the reel and belt (2b).</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2045281.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[15,1,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Check that the seat belt is\nundamaged.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/768.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000166.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>If the seat belt has been subjected\nto great stress, e.g. following an accident, it must be replaced\nas a complete unit together with its anchorages and the retaining\nbolts. Even if the seat belt does not show signs of visible defects,\nit may have lost its resistent properties.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><p>Fit the winder.</p><p>Tighten the winder retaining bolt.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>REAR SEAT BELT REEL.</p></td><td><p>M7/16&#x27;</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>4.0</p></td></tr></table></div><p>Position the idler and fasten it using\nthe bolt.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>REAR SEAT BELT IDLER..</p></td><td><p>7/16&quot;</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>4.0</p></td></tr></table></div><p>Position the centre idler and fasten it\nusing the bolt.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>REAR SEAT BELT IDLER..</p></td><td><p>7/16&quot;</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>4.0</p></td></tr></table></div><p>Close the idler cover.</p><p><a href=\"#/2429595\">7040H42</a></p><p><a href=\"#/2429589\">7040G30</a></p><p><a href=\"#/2429597\">7040H50</a>\n                                           (left\nside)</p><p><a href=\"#/2429642\">7050A10</a></p><p><a href=\"#/2429644\">7050A20</a></p><p><a href=\"#/2429604\">7040L40</a></p>"]]